& [P7P9SharedBoundaryImportAndAuthorityGapInventoryV1] is the P7P9-DR01 output for shared downstream reentry boundary import
  + [slice_id] is P7P9-DR01
  + [slice_status] is completed_for_review
  + [model_route_used] is requires deeper reasoning
  + [model_route_reason] is shared authority gaps decide the safe order for coordination contracts, dispatch refusal, operations-manager safety, and future live-control reconsideration
  + [authority_basis] is docs/canonical/LangSOP_Post_P6_Surface_Implementation_Downstream_Reentry.canonical.sop
  + [authority_basis_sha256] is 8B2B13EDDD722EA620CE0886CB24BB4CACC35FEE111C134EEB93DAEFBFB1A0BE
  + [slice_surface] is docs/slices/P7_P9_Downstream_Reentry_Final_Slices.v1.sop
  + [slice_surface_sha256] is F068D0A6FCE7B273AC5D3D770D1FDA397706430B4F5304F6E52C5D25818A19F2

  = must: provide the shared boundary for P7 and P9 without creating P7/P9 contracts beyond gap inventory
  = must: preserve the distinction between source authority, canonical authority, projections, carriers, manager packets, work packets, operation requests, dry-run results, human approval displays, generated outputs, and live effects
  = must: open P7P9-DR02 only after completion review accepts this output
  - never: authorize assignment, dispatch, operations control, live machine control, mailbox IO, adapters, transports, UI, dependency installation, package metadata mutation, command execution, process control, GPU control, model runtime mutation, job dispatch, credential access, network mutation, destructive filesystem action, or persistent operations automation

& [AcceptedBoundaryInput: P6SurfaceImplementation] is imported as projection and no-live-effect support
  + [source] is docs/planning/P6_Surface_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [source_sha256] is 981FC13220B30E20F2D296A7580E73739050DC363A7A923515745EAC0218A81F
  + [source] is docs/reviews/P6_Surface_Implementation_Completion_Review.v1.sop
  + [source_sha256] is ADB8E0B6A9AC26FD59CC5DC8391AD6C118FBAB87989C9B5D03DAFCC37071731D
  + [source] is docs/planning/Post_P6_Surface_Implementation_Readiness_Surface.v1.sop
  + [source_sha256] is 7BEBE692F0192DFE9D31E7D7B9B3B3F86909DA064895D617DFA2C7F355CD7055
  + [accepted_support] is surface projections can display authority notices, freshness notices, no-dispatch notices, no-operations-control notices, and no-live-effect notices
  + [accepted_support] is inbound surface action classification can distinguish user intent, manager packet, carrier state, and refused authority promotion
  + [accepted_support] is generated projections remain disposable and non-authoritative
  + [accepted_limit] is P6 does not authorize IRC, Matrix, browser, web, Codex, terminal, Langflow, MCP, adapter, transport, UI, assignment, dispatch, operations control, or live-control implementation

  = must: let P7 use P6 only for projection semantics and surface participation boundaries
  = must: let P9 use P6 only for no-live-effect and no-dispatch proof support

& [AcceptedBoundaryInput: CoordinationEvidence] is imported as P7 coordination support
  + [source] is docs/planning/IR6_Coordination_Mailbox_Projection_Prototype_Implementation_Proof_Pack.v1.sop
  + [source_sha256] is EE2BB9CB263D9284E42F79F4529B96AB9A09637D696B0F75A8100EC5AE44568C
