  + [accepted_support] is live-control safety specification, dry-run-before-live rule, explicit human approval requirement, rollback expectation, credential boundary, network boundary, and operations fault routing are standing safety constraints
  + [accepted_limit] is operations safety support does not by itself authorize live resource operations

  = must: treat FSC5 as the safety ceiling for all P9 planning
  = must: require separate future source-preserved SJS safety authority before any live-control reconsideration

& [AuthorityClassGapInventory] is the shared distinction map that P7/P9 must preserve
  + [authority_class] is source_document
    + [current_support] is preserved source and manifest records exist for downstream reentry
    + [gap_state] is no gap for planning; future source changes require reprocessing
  + [authority_class] is canonical_specification
    + [current_support] is SJS-signed canonical downstream reentry specification exists
    + [gap_state] is no gap for P7P9-DR01 through P7P9-DR10 planning order
  + [authority_class] is projection_surface
    + [current_support] is P6 surface implementation can project authority and freshness notices
    + [gap_state] is P7/P9 must define participant and carrier semantics before new surfaces are trusted
  + [authority_class] is conversation_carrier
    + [current_support] is IR6 mailbox carrier proof and P6 cross-surface projection evidence exist
    + [gap_state] is IRC, Matrix, web, browser, Codex, terminal, mailbox IO, and Langflow carriers lack implementation authority
  + [authority_class] is coordination_claim
    + [current_support] is IR6 claim proof exists
    + [gap_state] is P7 must restate participant identity, claim compatibility, stale claim review, and human override under the broader multi-user/multi-agent surface model
  + [authority_class] is assignment_candidate
    + [current_support] is IR8 work packet candidate records exist
    + [gap_state] is assignment candidate is not assignment authority and requires P7 dispatch refusal contract
  + [authority_class] is dispatch_authority
    + [current_support] is none
    + [gap_state] is intentionally blocked until separate source-preserved SJS authority exists
  + [authority_class] is operation_request
    + [current_support] is IR7 dry-run request evidence and IR8 operations handoff evidence exist
    + [gap_state] is P9 must restate operations-manager request identity and refusal semantics before runtime planning
  + [authority_class] is dry_run_result
    + [current_support] is IR7 dry-run result proof exists
    + [gap_state] is dry-run success is not live approval and must remain non-authoritative
  + [authority_class] is human_approval_display
    + [current_support] is operations safety approval requirements exist
    + [gap_state] is P9 must define freshness, expiration, revocation, scope, and audit before any future live-control activation can be proposed
  + [authority_class] is live_control_authority
    + [current_support] is none
    + [gap_state] is intentionally blocked until separate source-preserved safety authority, dry-run proof, least-privilege boundary, rollback proof, monitor proof, emergency stop, and explicit human approval model are accepted

  = must: preserve the authority_class gap inventory as an input to P7P9-DR02 through P7P9-DR08
  = must: reject future packets that collapse assignment_candidate into dispatch_authority or dry_run_result into live_control_authority

& [P7ReadinessGapSet] is the coordination gap set opened by this boundary import
  + [gap] is participant identity and conversation identity must be widened from IR6 to multi-user and multi-agent surfaces
  + [gap] is authority class contract must distinguish human user, agent, manager, worker, tool, automation, surface, carrier, source, projection, generated output, claim, packet, operation request, and approval display
  + [gap] is work claim and assignment candidate semantics must preserve dispatch refusal
  + [gap] is cross-surface carrier and rendezvous projection must support IRC, Matrix, web, Codex, terminal, browser, mailbox, Langflow, and narrative surfaces without making any protocol source truth
  + [gap] is conflict, staleness, human override, release, supersession, and completion review must be restated for multi-agent and multi-surface participation
  + [blocked_scope] is mailbox IO, IRC adapter, Matrix adapter, web adapter, browser adapter, Codex adapter, terminal adapter, Langflow export, UI implementation, assignment, dispatch, and automatic conflict resolution

  = must: route P7P9-DR02 through P7P9-DR05 to deeper reasoning

& [P9ReadinessGapSet] is the operations-manager safety gap set opened by this boundary import
  + [gap] is resource taxonomy must classify process, GPU, model runtime, job, file, credential, network, automation, scheduler, monitor, and external service targets
  + [gap] is operations-manager request and dry-run result semantics must preserve no-live-effect and dispatch refusal
  + [gap] is approval, credential, network, rollback, and emergency-stop semantics must be stated before any future live-control reconsideration
  + [gap] is generated output and fixture oracle plan must prove no promotion from dry-run success to live approval
  + [gap] is future Ryzen 9 RTX 5090 management remains deferred until separate signed safety activation, least-privilege credentials, monitors, rollback, and emergency stop exist
  + [blocked_scope] is runtime scheduler, resource monitor, GPU controller, process controller, model-runtime manager, job controller, credential manager, network manager, persistent automation, command execution, operations control, and live machine control

  = must: route P7P9-DR06 through P7P9-DR08 to deeper reasoning
  = must: treat P7P9-DR09 as GPT-5.3-Codex-Spark-suitable only after P7P9-DR01 through P7P9-DR08 are accepted

